\section*{Rivers and Settlements}

9KASS08

\section*{8.1 Why Settlements Follow Rivers}

The earliest villages of our state grew along river banks. A river gives
drinking water, soft soil for farming, fish for food, and an easy path for
boats. Where a river slows and widens, markets appeared, and some of those
markets became towns.

